    702  f0bf							; --- VDEL: P0 ON, P1 OFF. NOT the HUD's 13+2 usage — this is the cave's
    703  f0bf							; one-line-ahead discipline, and it is x-INDEPENDENT only when the landing
    704  f0bf							; point of the write is RIGHT of every sprite pixel.
    705  f0bf							; Facts (Stella `Player::grp` / `updatePattern`): without VDEL a GRP write
    706  f0bf							; lands in `myPatternNew` and is rendered immediately, so a mid-line write
    707  f0bf							; affects the CURRENT line when the sprite has not started yet (its pixels
    708  f0bf							; begin at cycle ~(61+X)/3) and the NEXT line otherwise. `myPatternOld`,
    709  f0bf							; the VDEL slot, is latched when the OTHER player is written
    710  f0bf							; (`shufflePatterns`), so VDEL does NOT delay by a line on its own — it
    711  f0bf							; moves the landing point to the other register's store cycle.
    712  f0bf							; Measured store phases (`tools/cycle_ledger.py`, P1 worst path):
    713  f0bf							;   COLUP0 c19 (< all pixels: the per-row colour is always this line),
    714  f0bf							;   GRP0 c35, GRP1 c58, COLUP1 c65.
    715  f0bf							; P0: VDELP0=1 moves its landing from GRP0's c35 (= correct art only for
    716  f0bf							;   X < 44 px) to GRP1's c58 (X < 113 px) and, in the same stroke, aligns
    717  f0bf							;   the art with PlayerColTable (today art row r sits one line above its
    718  f0bf							;   colour for X >= 44). P1 keep VDELP1=0: its latch would be GRP0's c35,
    719  f0bf							;   i.e. a WORSE split than today's c58, and P1's colour would stay at c65.
    720  f0bf							; Every .Line body writes GRP1 exactly once on every path (.Grp1 in-window
    721  f0bf							; or .ObjNoRes blank), so the P0 latch is driven every scanline; that is
    722  f0bf							; the contract `tools/test_vdel_cave.py` guards. HERO clears both bits at
    723  f0bf							; cave entry and uses VDEL only for its HUD text, so this is the one place
    724  f0bf							; we deliberately differ (measured, not guessed).
    725  f0bf		       a9 01		      lda	#1
    726  f0c1		       85 25		      sta	VDELP0
    727  f0c3		       a9 00		      lda	#0
    728  f0c5		       85 26		      sta	VDELP1
    729  f0c7		       85 1f		      sta	ENABL	; HUD-bar leftover off before first visible
    730  f0c9							;   line (.Row row0 BandTab rewrites next)
