   1778  f4ed							; Room exit handlers — check connection table, switch rooms, reposition player
   1779  f4ed							; ==============================================================================
   1780  f4ed							; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   1781  f4ed							; C3 (2026-10-20): the four handlers MOVED to bank2 ($FC4F cluster) — the
   1782  f4ed							; connection table is level data in bank2, so each handler now reads its own
   1783  f4ed							; 2-byte conn record directly (bank1 GetConnIdx + FoldIndirect hops gone).
   1784  f4ed							; bank0 keeps only the entry pads at $FBD9-$FBE4 (3 B each, `sta $1FF8`;
   1785  f4ed							; bank2 serves the `jmp` at A+3). The OPPOSITE-EDGE placement is written
   1786  f4ed							; BEFORE `jmp EnterRoomB2`, because EnterRoom never touches RoomX/RoomY
   1787  f4ed							; (checked: EnterRoomB2 + B3RoomBlocks read neither) — that keeps the whole
   1788  f4ed							; tail in bank2 with 0 pushes: EnterRoomB2's `jmp ReturnPad` pops the
   1789  f4ed							; ORIGINAL `jsr ExitRoomXxx` frame, exactly like the old in-bank return.
   1790  f4ed							; Guard: verify_build.CORRIDOR_PADS (4 pads) + check_exit_handlers (edge
   1791  f4ed							; placement precedes the EnterRoomB2 tail; no-exit path ends in ReturnPad).
   1792  f4ed							; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   1793  f4ed
