   1795  f4ed							; Level management
   1796  f4ed							; ==============================================================================
   1797  f4ed							; LoadLevel MOVED to bank2 (C2, 2026-10-20) — body = LoadLevelB2 ($F640).
   1798  f4ed							; The level index/table lives in bank2 (level data), so the old body paid 7
   1799  f4ed							; `jsr FoldIndirect` (7 x 25c + 14 bank switches) to read a 7-byte entry that
   1800  f4ed							; an in-bank (FetchPtr),Y read now fetches directly. Both halves are split
   1801  f4ed							; pads (same discipline as CallPad_SelectObject):
   1802  f4ed							;   A=$FC20  CallPad_LoadLevel / LoadLevel: `sta $1FF8`   (bank0 runs this)
   1803  f4ed							;   A+3=$FC23	bank2 `jmp LoadLevelB2` 		   (fetched after it)
   1804  f4ed							;   body tail `jmp $FC26` -> bank2 `sta $1FF6` at $FC26 -> the fetch at $FC29
   1805  f4ed							;   comes from HERE: `jmp LF_B0Tail`, i.e. the drop-in tail (EnterRoom call,
   1806  f4ed							;   level-start placement, `jmp DropArm`) stays in bank0 so the call chain and
   1807  f4ed							;   the measured stack depth are UNCHANGED (0 extra jsr levels, 0 pushes).
   1808  f4ed							; Entry layout: stride 7 = miner_room (b7 = faces right), miner_x, wall color,
   1809  f4ed							; wall color 2, block base word (RoomShapes), room count n (the RoomPositions
   1810  f4ed							; /RoomCounts/enemy-record bases are that block's +n/+2n/+3n offsets, C2).
   1811  f4ed							; Guards: verify_build.check_callpads pins the entry pad bytes + operand,
   1812  f4ed							; check_loadlevel_tramp pins the return half; tools/test_respawn_hover.py,
   1813  f4ed							; test_room_dark.py and test_level_bank.py read the bank2 body.
   1814  f4ed
