   3210  fc20							; ENTRY: a bank0 caller `jsr LoadLevel` lands on `sta $1FF8` here; the opcode
   3211  fc20							; fetch at $FC23 then comes from bank2 = `jmp LoadLevelB2` (split-pad rule).
   3212  fc20							; The three bank0 bytes at $FC23-$FC25 are NEVER fetched (bank2's jmp lives
   3213  fc20							; there) — zero-filled so nothing can branch into them by accident.
   3214  fc20							; RETURN: the body's tail is `jmp $FC26`; bank2's $FC26 holds `sta $1FF6`, so
   3215  fc20							; the fetch at $FC29 lands on the `jmp LF_B0Tail` below (live bank0 half).
   3216  fc20							; Guard: verify_build.check_callpads (entry pad) + check_loadlevel_tramp
   3217  fc20							; (return half + this stub's shape).
