   3788  fe14							; ==============================================================================
   3789  fe14							; Phase 5 — second GRP1 object (no flicker). TIA has one GRP1 sprite, so two
   3790  fe14							; objects in a room used to alternate frames (30 Hz flicker each). When they
   3791  fe14							; live in DIFFERENT cave bands each can be drawn on ALL of its scanlines: the
   3792  fe14							; band's setup swaps the live trio (ObjBase/ObjTop/ActiveObjectX) for slot 1
   3793  fe14							; and repositions P1 there. The per-line object path is untouched — it already
   3794  fe14							; draws from the live trio and takes COLUP1 from ObjColorTab[ObjBase+row].
   3795  fe14							;
   3796  fe14							; Invariant (do not relax): slot 1's band is STRICTLY HIGHER than slot 0's.
   3797  fe14							; Bands are set up 0->1->2, so no later band has to restore slot 0's trio.
   3798  fe14							; Rooms whose two objects share a band keep the old behaviour (slot 0 only,
   3799  fe14							; rotation in SelectActiveObject unchanged).
   3800  fe14							; Cost: the band-compare early-out sits in the setup line's free tail (0
   3801  fe14							; lines); a band that DOES host slot 1 pays 2 lines (SetObjectXPos must start
   3802  fe14							; on a line boundary and the HMOVE needs the next line's HBLANK).
   3803  fe14							;
   3804  fe14							; StageSlot1 (VBLANK, after SelectActiveObject): stages ObjBase1/ObjTop1/ObjX1,
   3805  fe14							; $FF = none. Slot 1 = the miner or the first live enemy whose Y is in a band
   3806  fe14							; above slot 0's. The KEY skip mirrors the slot-0 path (KeyHeld = LevelStartRoom
   3807  fe14							; b7). Tally frames ($FE) are gated out: EnemyRamY holds score-pointer bytes
   3808  fe14							; then (AGENTS: tally frame draws the MINER only).
   3809  fe14							; ==============================================================================
   3810  fe14
   3811  fe14		       00 00 00 00*	      .ds	$FE90 - *, 0	; ObjColorTab/ObjSprites moved to the
   3812  fe90							; $F744 fill (Phase 6: tall art). The $FE8F
   3813  fe90							; end is kept so FoldIndirect stays at $FE90.
   3814  fe90							; BOTH same-page 4c fetches (verify guards);
   3815  fe90							; end $FE8F -> HOF tramp $FE90 (shifted +$10,
   3816  fe90							; mirrors+HOF_ENTRY/LHT_ENTRY synced)
   3817  fe90							; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   3818  fe90							; ObjColorTab — per-scanline GRP1 object colors, stride 8 = ObjSprites
   3819  fe90							; stride; indexed by the same X = ObjBase + r in .Grp1 at $FE00 (4c, same
   3820  fe90							; page for all 72 B — the passing +7 probe's exact cycle sum). Row colors
   3821  fe90							; per OBJ_* slot: type color x8 (matches EnemyColorTable /
   3822  fe90							; SelectActiveObject frame colors — no visual change for enemies/lamp/bomb);
   3823  fe90							; MINER slot = miner.png purple/pink/grey -> nearest NTSC $54/$4A/$08.
   3824  fe90							; NOTE: dark rooms no longer force grey objects — the frame-level $0A write
   3825  fe90							; is overridden per row (no budget for a dark skip flag; see .Line probe).
   3826  fe90							; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   3827  fe90
   3828  fe90							; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   3829  fe90							; FoldIndirect — cross-bank data fetch (HERO fold, write-triggered;
   3830  fe90							; level_bank_plan §0.1). Pad lands $FEF6-$FEFF (last byte ≤ $FEFF — $FF00
   3831  fe90							; stays the fineAdjust anchor). Bytes must be byte-identical in bank2
   3832  fe90							; (guard: verify_build) — after `sta $1FF8` the CPU fetches the remainder
   3833  fe90							; from the data bank at the same PC.
   3834  fe90							; Contract: bank select is ABSOLUTE $1FF8 (bank2) — X/Y both preserved,
   3835  fe90							; A = junk in, data out (`sta $1FF6` switches back, A preserved).
   3836  fe90							; P3.1 deviation (plan §0): `sta $1FF8,X` required X=0, but every enemy
   3837  fe90							; loop keeps the slot in X and has no free temp to swap (DEY/snake hold
   3838  fe90							; Temp live across the read). All level data is bank2, so X-selection is
